# MetaLandRoad: incremental, in-place code

- **MetaRoad** = target/reference plugin; **MetaLandRoad** = this project plugin.
- Full text: skill `metal-androad-incremental-dev` and `Docs/Agent-Conventions.md`.
- Any Editor Mode / Interactive Tool: `Docs/UE-InteractiveTool-Standard.md` (`OnClickPress` dispatches only).
- Runtime vs Editor packaging: `Docs/MetaLandRoad-Runtime-Editor.md`. Runtime = data/mesh/stamp; Editor = Tool/Mode/Visualizer. Runtime calls Editor only via `FMetaLandRoadEditorHooks`.

## Review

- Audit first: mark `[审核]` (location, why it is wrong, suggested result).
- Dead / unused (hotkeys, preview, `#if 0`, leftover MetaRoad accessors): mark, **ask 是否移除**, do not delete until yes. Do not attach new features to a marked dead path.
- Lane/Section live API = index + SOffset. Do not keep unused `GetStartSection` / object-ref wrappers or `static Fallback` refs. Symmetric Pin/Unpin: mark first.
- Do not silently rewrite. Discuss, then change only agreed items.
- No line-count split rule. Split by **one file, one story**, after user OK.

## C++ style

- **`.h`**: declarations. **`.cpp`**: all function bodies.
- File-local `static` and anonymous namespace in `.cpp` are OK.
- No `namespace XxxPrivate` as a second module. No new one-off `*Utils` / `*Generation` files.
- New `UCLASS` / Tool / Global Shader → new file is normal.
- Prefer small compile-safe slices.

## Product / junction

- Landscape params = height only. Road weight falloff = Landscape Key (0 = Actor default); junction uses Actor. Profile PS draws Road only.
- Visible road spans = `GetJunctionMeshGenerationSpans` (single owner).
- **Figure 1** + vertex-order audit on every junction publish; fail → abort.
- Junction cook: `Docs/MetaLandRoad-Junction-Spec.md` (T / Cross / N). Same-spline = outer chord, never inward fillet. Do not fix N by changing T (or the reverse).
- Body-corner loft sweeps the authored spline (`Center + Right × Off`). Do not replace PathCenter with a second fillet curve (`Docs/MetaLandRoad-Guidance-vs-Mesh-Review.md`).
- 4→5 / N-way = whole-node recook, not local patches. After a cook change, Recook T far-half + Cross/Fig2 + one 5-way.
